{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bwjrmgj4l","tool_use_id":"toolu_017tkhR3xraRE17ZpciQ9Tyy","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/6bc82155-43f8-41fc-800b-5352bc149f5f/tasks/bwjrmgj4l.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_5\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built.py\necho local_alternation_switch_ideal_rule > $D/model_name.txt\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nRefinement of `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built` (tally span judged against a personal expected span, switching judged by closeness to a personal ideal switching rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, a personal left/right lean). The one change: people notice a local stretch of strict alternation (HTHT or THTH within any four consecutive flips) as a visible pattern in its own right, and every such alternating four-flip stretch counts against a sequence's randomness through a shared penalty scaled by the person's pattern sensitivity — even when the whole sequence is not rule-built and its overall switching rate is near their ideal. Of two sequences with the same number of switches, people therefore pick the one whose switches are not bunched into extended alternation, addressing the critique that among equal-switch pairs people choose the sequence with fewer alternating four-flip windows more often than the best model predicts.\nEOF\npython3 - \"$SRC\" \"$D/candidate.py\" << 'PY'\nimport sys\ns=open(sys.argv[1]).read()\ndoc_end=s.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\ns='''\"\"\"Local strict-alternation penalty in the person-specific switch-ideal rule-built judgement.\n\nRefinement of `person_switch_ideal_pattern_rule_built` (tally span against a\npersonal expected span, switching by closeness to a personal ideal switching\nrate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern\nsensitivity, a personal left/right lean). The one change: every four-flip\nstretch of strict alternation (HTHT / THTH) is noticed as a visible pattern\nand counts against randomness, by a shared penalty scaled by the person's\npattern sensitivity, so of two sequences with equal switch counts people pick\nthe one with fewer alternating four-flip stretches.\n\"\"\"'''+s[doc_end:]\ns=s.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def alt_windows(seq):\n        # Number of four-flip windows that strictly alternate (HTHT / THTH).\n        return float(sum(1 for i in range(len(seq) - 3) if seq[i:i + 4] in (\"HTHT\", \"THTH\")))\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\ns=s.replace('''        \"log_len\":''','''        \"alt_diff\": alt_windows(a) - alt_windows(b),\n        \"log_len\":''')\ns=s.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(''','''    alt_diff = pm.Data(\"alt_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_len = pm.Data(''')\ns=s.replace('''    # Person-specific pattern sensitivity''','''    # The change: shared penalty per strictly alternating four-flip window.\n    alpha = pm.Normal(\"alpha\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n\n    # Person-specific pattern sensitivity''')\ns=s.replace(\"(gamma * trip_diff - rho * rule_diff)\",\"(gamma * trip_diff - rho * rule_diff - alpha * alt_diff)\")\nopen(sys.argv[2],'w').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -n alt $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"faa96c93-afcd-4b85-8367-9ba9cba00624","session_id":"6bc82155-43f8-41fc-800b-535